Package: pretty-terminal
Version: 0.2.1
Section: x11
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Pretty Authors <dev@pretty.local>
Homepage: https://github.com/mappingAu/pretty
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.35), libgcc-s1, libfontconfig1, libfreetype6, libxkbcommon0, libxkbcommon-x11-0, libwayland-client0, libwayland-cursor0, libwayland-egl1, libx11-6, libx11-xcb1, libxcb1, libxcursor1, libxi6, libxrandr2, libxfixes3, libxext6, libegl1, libvulkan1
Recommends: fonts-jetbrains-mono, fonts-noto-color-emoji, fonts-noto-cjk
Installed-Size: 30000
Description: Hardware accelerated, kitty-compatible terminal emulator
 Pretty is a GPU accelerated terminal emulator using Vulkan or OpenGL ES 3.0+
 through wgpu. It implements the kitty graphics protocol, kitty keyboard
 protocol, OSC 8 hyperlinks, OSC 52 clipboard, desktop notifications, true
 color, ligatures, scrollback, tiling panes and KDE/X11 compositor blur.
 Metal (macOS) and Direct3D 12 (Windows) are supported native backends.
